        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · South &amp; Southeast Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Plassey</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">23 June 1757; the fighting is said to have ended in approximately 11 hours</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Palashi (Anglicised Plassey) on the banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hooghly-river">Hooghly River</a>, about 150 kilometres (93 mi) north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> and south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murshidabad">Murshidabad</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-bengal">West Bengal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> under Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive">Robert Clive</a>, with about 3,000 soldiers (some 750 European infantry, 2,100 sepoys and artillery), and a small French contingent on the other side; the Nawab Siraj-ud-Daulah, with about 50,000 soldiers including the defectors (30,000 infantry and 20,000 cavalry by the fuller count), 10 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>, and artillery put at anything from 40 to 300 pieces.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Nawab's army dispersed and Siraj-ud-Daulah fled; the Company occupied his camp. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-clive">Clive</a> estimated the Nawab's losses at 500 men, and British losses were estimated at 22 killed and 50 wounded, with 13 sepoys killed and 30 wounded.</span></div>
        </div>
